1
00:05:25,714 --> 00:05:31,714
Long ago he made a deal to save someone he loved.

2
00:10:51,428 --> 00:10:57,428
Ghost Rider is a thriller, action, fantasy film directed by Mark Steven Johnson.

3
00:16:17,142 --> 00:16:23,142
In order to save his dying father, young stunt cyclist Johnny Blaze sells his soul to
Mephistopheles and sadly parts from the pure-hearted Roxanne Simpson, the love of his life.

4
00:21:42,857 --> 00:21:48,857
Years later, Johnny's path crosses again with Roxanne, now a go-getting reporter, and also with
Mephistopheles, who offers to release Johnny's soul if Johnny becomes the fabled, fiery 'Ghost Rider'.

5
00:27:08,571 --> 00:27:14,571
Johnny Blaze / Ghost Rider, played by Nicolas Cage.

6
00:32:34,285 --> 00:32:40,285
Roxanne Simpson, played by Eva Mendes.

7
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Carter Slade / Phantom Rider, played by Sam Elliott.

8
00:43:25,714 --> 00:43:31,714
Blackheart / Black King, played by Wes Bentley.

9
00:48:51,428 --> 00:48:57,428
Mephistopheles / Mephisto, played by Peter Fonda.

10
00:54:17,142 --> 00:54:23,142
Young Johnny Blaze, played by Matt Long.

11
00:59:42,857 --> 00:59:48,857
Ghost Rider is a 2007 American superhero film written
and directed by Mark Steven Johnson.

12
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
Based on the Marvel Comics character of the same name, it was produced by Columbia Pictures in association with Marvel
Entertainment, Crystal Sky Pictures, and Relativity Media, and distributed by Sony Pictures Releasing.

13
01:10:34,285 --> 01:10:40,285
The film stars Nicolas Cage as the titular character, with Eva Mendes, Wes Bentley, Sam
Elliott, Donal Logue, Matt Long, and Peter Fonda in supporting roles.

14
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film follows Johnny Blaze, a motorcycle stuntman who sells his soul and
becomes the Ghost Rider, a bounty hunter of evil demons.

15
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
Ghost Rider was released on February 16, 2007, in the United States.

16
01:26:51,428 --> 01:26:57,428
The film was met with negative reviews from critics and grossed
$228.7 million worldwide against a $110 million budget.

17
01:32:17,142 --> 01:32:23,142
Ghost Rider was released on DVD, Blu-ray and UMD on June 12, 2007.

18
01:37:42,857 --> 01:37:48,857
A sequel, titled Ghost Rider: Spirit of Vengeance, was released on
February 17, 2012, with Cage reprising his role.

19
01:43:08,571 --> 01:43:14,571
The film explores themes of dying and death, religion and
supernatural, superhero, possession, devil's son.

20
01:48:34,285 --> 01:48:40,285
The tone is intense.
